From 1c49cf34d02f7ef0113abad849f43074036af3a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:25:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] Back off on throttled responses below the SDK retries

The SDKs retry 429/5xx a few times within seconds (google-genai's
Interactions client: 3 retries at 0.5-8 s), and _request_with_retries then
spends MAX_RETRIES without waiting, so a short congestion window ends a run
with AGENT_ERROR. Gemini Flex answers 503 at capacity and 429 for rate
limits and asks clients to implement their own exponential backoff
(https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/flex-inference).

- ThrottleBackoffTransport (benchmarking/runtime_transport.py) wraps the
  SDK client's httpx transport and retries throttled responses (default
  429, 503) with exponential backoff and jitter, honouring Retry-After.
  The SDK never sees a retried response, so neither SDK retries nor
  MAX_RETRIES are spent. Action and harness summary requests are covered.
- Waiting is bounded per throttled episode (max_wait_seconds) and by the
  run's wall-clock deadline; past either bound the throttled response is
  passed through. A model call that then fails after the deadline ends
  the run with TIME_BUDGET instead of AGENT_ERROR.
- Opt-in per config as client.transport_retry (validated, extra keys
  rejected). build_model_runtime_client accepts http_transport and passes
  it to the google-genai (HttpOptions.client_args), OpenAI and Anthropic
  (DefaultHttpxClient) clients; without the block clients are built
  exactly as before.
- run_meta.json records the policy and counters as transport_retry.
- The four Gemini 3.8 Flash high path profiles enable the same policy
  (2 s initial, 60 s max delay, 30 min per episode), so the setting is
  identical across the path. Request bodies are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
